https://github.com/microsoft/terminal/blob/fb597ed304ec6eef245405c9652e9b8a029b821f/src/cascadia/TerminalApp/Pane.LayoutSizeNode.cpp#L56-L73

`nodeField.release();` **This call does not destroy the managed object**, but the unique_ptr object is released from the responsibility of deleting the object. Some other entity must take responsibility for deleting the object at some point. Unfortunately, we lose the pointer to the managed object. **So finally, the memory leak will occur. The correct way is `nodeField.reset();`** . See [std::unique_ptr::release](http://www.cplusplus.com/reference/memory/unique_ptr/release/) .
In my opinion, the most simple and correct solution for `Pane::LayoutSizeNode::_AssignChildNode` is:
```cpp
void Pane::LayoutSizeNode::_AssignChildNode(std::unique_ptr<LayoutSizeNode>& nodeField, const LayoutSizeNode* const newNode)
{
	nodeField = newNode ? std::make_unique<LayoutSizeNode>(*newNode) : nullptr;
}
```
